{
  "borough": "Harrow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The development, by reason of proposed lightwell, would result in inadequate daylight/sunlight, poor outlook to bedrooms 1 and 2, and the lack of defensible space between the living room window and car parking area in the fornt forecourt of the property,&amp;nbsp; would result in substandard living accommodation for future occupiers of the site and would give rise to loss of privacy, outlook and amenity to the occupants to the detriment of their living conditions. The development is thereby contrary to the high quality design aspirations of the National Planning Policy Framework (2021), Policies D3.D(7), (9), (10), D6.C, D6.F (3) and (8), and H9 of The London Plan (2021), Policies DM1 A, DM1 C, DM1 D (f), (g), (h), (i), DM27 A and C, DM30 A (b) and (c) of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013) and the adopted Supplementary Planning Documents Residential Design Guide (2010).&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;&quot;&gt;In\r\nthe absence of any supporting information or justification, the loss of\r\nvaluable small office space&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;for which there is an identified local need, in a highly accessible location and adjacent to a\r\ndistrict centre,&amp;nbsp; would impact the overall\r\navailability of the required office stock for the local area; contrary to the\r\naspirations of the National Planning Policy Framework (2021); Policy CS.1B of\r\nthe Harrow Core Strategy (2012); Policy E1 of London Plan (2021) &amp;amp; Policy\r\nDM32 of the Development Management Plan Local Policies (2013).&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
